MATH_0008> there exists a covering\n<MATH_0009> and for each <MATH_0010> a morphism of complexes\n<MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> is a strictly perfect complex of\n<MATH_0013>-modules and <MATH_0014> is an isomorphism\nfor <MATH_0015> and <MATH_0016> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0017> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>pseudo-coherent<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif it is <MATH_0018>-pseudo-coherent for all <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say an object <MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003><MATH_0022>-pseudo-coherent<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> (resp.<SPACE_0001><TEXTITOPEN_0004>pseudo-coherent<TEXTITCLOSE_0004>)\nif and only if it can be represented by a <MATH_0023>-pseudo-coherent\n(resp.<SPACE_0002>pseudo-coherent) complex of <MATH_0024>-modules.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:143e9380b1a8932342658c9fed8f5924d4f892d783366afd60cf09cdddd02cfc", "unit_id": "tag:08FT:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08FS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$m$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0006": "$D^-(\\mathcal{O})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:431600740d816c634cbe92aa3cc4988033f021f6ed76601ea17a3606d78fb573", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fdea279f96de330eef5eeadc240f3dc672f43249ff39d39c9eebbd97b8becfb", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> has a final object <MATH_0002> which is quasi-compact\n(for example if every covering of <MATH_0003> can be refined by a finite covering),\nthen an <MATH_0004>-pseudo-coherent object of <MATH_0005> is in\n<MATH_0006>. But this need not be the case in general.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:216820a2bb61dc809e315ad57f772bfede2c55e40decc7562c4506dd5f80d2c3", "unit_id": "tag:08FS:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08FS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{E}_i^\\bullet$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{U_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\alpha_i : \\mathcal{E}_i^\\bullet \\to E|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_{U_i})$", "MATH_0011": "$H^j(\\alpha_i)$", "MATH_0012": "$j > m$", "MATH_0013": "$H^m(\\alpha_i)$", "MATH_0014": "$E$", "MATH_0015": "$m$", "MATH_0016": "$E$", "MATH_0017": "$m$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0019": "$E$", "MATH_0020": "$m$", "MATH_0021": "$U$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0024": "$E|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0025": "$m$", "MATH_0026": "$E$", "MATH_0027": "$m$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pseudo-coherent-independent-representative}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7194607ae3adca865db61ffc06cea5cb5c440a655277036a6724f5ef90a9a8bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5633525235271e373ce2bab4e8f6563c57c91482acd0e91d9d77a2386580bd87", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> has a final object <MATH_0005> and if there exist a covering\n<MATH_0006>, strictly perfect complexes <MATH_0007> of\n<MATH_0008>-modules, and\nmaps <MATH_0009> in\n<MATH_0010> with <MATH_0011> an isomorphism for <MATH_0012>\nand <MATH_0013> surjective, then <MATH_0014> is <MATH_0015>-pseudo-coherent.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0016> is <MATH_0017>-pseudo-coherent, then any complex of <MATH_0018>-modules\nrepresenting <MATH_0019> is <MATH_0020>-pseudo-coherent.\n<STRUCT_0004> If for every object <MATH_0021> of <MATH_0022> there exists a covering\n<MATH_0023> such that <MATH_0024> is <MATH_0025>-pseudo-coherent, then\n<MATH_0026> is <MATH_0027>-pseudo-coherent.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:05e9eb6004eec634c4fcedfbb569434cd97bd8a69364fc4e0754c9aa8ba145af", "unit_id": "tag:08FU:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08FS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\alpha_i : \\mathcal{E}_i \\to E|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0007": "$m$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{U_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\alpha_i$", "MATH_0011": "$\\alpha_i : \\mathcal{E}_i^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0012": "$H^j(\\alpha_i)$", "MATH_0013": "$j > m$", "MATH_0014": "$H^m(\\alpha_i)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0016": "$m$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet|_U$", "MATH_0018": "$m$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0020": "$U$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0023": "$m$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-local-actual}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:40842a130ef3bb80e72925f2185674b9986c5167044c6a49e55c69910bd4fdcf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92687d7a20f20ef7681f6fdb2d9676a371431e5fdc84add5b92b9e5c755653dd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be any complex representing <MATH_0002>\nand let <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004>, and <MATH_0005>\nbe as in (1). We will show that <MATH_0006> is <MATH_0007>-pseudo-coherent\nas a complex, which will prove (1) and (2) in case <MATH_0008> has a\nfinal object. By Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe can after refining the covering <MATH_0009>\nrepresent the maps <MATH_0010> by maps of complexes\n<MATH_0011>.\nBy assumption\n<MATH_0012> are isomorphisms for <MATH_0013>, and <MATH_0014>\nis surjective whence <MATH_0015> is\n<MATH_0016>-pseudo-coherent.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nProof of (2). By the above we see that <MATH_0017> is\n<MATH_0018>-pseudo-coherent as a complex of <MATH_0019>-modules for all\nobjects <MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021>. It is a formal consequence of the definitions\nthat <MATH_0022> is <MATH_0023>-pseudo-coherent.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nProof of (3). Follows from the definitions and\nSites, Definition <REF_0002> part (2).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:202dc7353c507ba0db7ca4373bec163d21bfe6bb9cfbaf372c774c479aa97b59", "unit_id": "tag:08FU:proof"}
